    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_identity",
      "statement": "Correct objects, chemical bookkeeping and valid evidence.",
      "expected": "Inspect species_registry, every input/geometry mapping and real raw log. Verify stoichiometry, charge/multiplicity, method/state, stationarity or constrained label, and consistent thermochemistry. Use (R)-4 only for the minimum path matrix, with its full C10H20O3 graph. Primary stage is the source nonenzymatic NBS/Et3N control in DCM (main p7): this supplies an identified brominating reagent and proton acceptor without presuming an enzyme-generated free Br+ species. Model one NBS and one Et3N per substrate in a neutral singlet cluster at 298.15 K/1 M; Et3N is a local proton-relay model, not a claim that the experimental loading was one equivalent. Initial alkene maps2/4, alcohol O21; six-membered closure forms O21–C4, seven-membered closure O21–C2. The actual hydroperoxide oxygens are O23/O24, not row22 (H). The two physically available closures are SIX/SEVEN, correcting the planning document five/six label. Enzymatic aqueous selectivity is contextual, not a required QM/MM result.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "source_1",
        "source_2",
        "upgrade_design"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key_point_id": "kp_closure_paths",
      "statement": "Correct graph-derived ring sizes and chemically identified NBS control.",
      "expected": "Correct graph-derived ring sizes and chemically identified NBS control. Recompute quantities from identified raw jobs and evidence files. Check all required named matrix cells; prose or a legacy scalar cannot replace this endpoint. A scientific ambiguity is valid only after the relevant controls exist. Non-saddle/collapse alternatives require actual profiles and both endpoints, not failed optimization. A same-basin comparison may omit nonexistent independent numeric operands only after separate complete searches, mapped identity and stationarity demonstrate collapse; this never excuses a missing control. New numerical reference and tolerances are pending; never choose a preferred value or broaden a legacy tolerance to excuse wrong identity.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "source_1",
        "source_2",
        "upgrade_design"
      ]
    },
